{
  "_comment": "Cross-language parity fixture for river generation (RiverGenerator.Generate backend / generateRivers frontend): given a synthetic island's tiles (with terrain), a world seed, an island index, and wasted/allowConfluence flags, both sides must trace the same rivers in the same order. Covers: a small green island with one simple spring-straight-mouth river, a green island whose two traced rivers collide into a confluence, a green island whose river takes at least one sharp (bend60) turn, and a wasted island whose lava stream (allowConfluence: false) never merges. Every scenario's tiles/terrain, seed, island index and wasted flag were taken from a real WorldGenerator.Generate() run (so terrain, depth-field noise and the actual river trace all agree byte-for-byte with what that seed really produces), not hand-crafted. RiverGenerationGoldenTests.cs (backend) and riverGenerator.golden.test.ts (frontend) each compute against this fixture using their own production river-tracing implementation, then assert the frozen `rivers` list below (order matters: sorted by (q, r), same as RiverGenerator.BuildRiverTiles's own output order).",
